WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.710 --> 00:00:06.200
Good news, Amazon Prime subscribers: September
2019 brings plenty of westerns, two Mad Max

00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:11.410
films, gateways to the stars, presidents fighting
terrorists in the sky, kaiju and Arnold Schwarzenegger

00:00:11.480 --> 00:00:12.880
breaking faces on Mars.

00:00:12.980 --> 00:00:14.200
Here's the best of what's ahead.

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:19.839
The edgy action-drama series The Family Man
stars the renowned Indian actor Manoj Bajpayee

00:00:19.839 --> 00:00:24.269
as an undercover operative who works for a
government intelligence agency trying to take

00:00:24.269 --> 00:00:26.100
down terrorist groups from the inside.

00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:29.849
The Family Man looks not only at the danger
he faces working for the government, but how

00:00:29.849 --> 00:00:32.500
he balances that work with his demanding family
life.

00:00:32.680 --> 00:00:37.420
In August 2019, India West reported The Family
Man was the first Indian television series

00:00:37.420 --> 00:00:40.660
to be showcased by Los Angeles' Television
Critics Association.

00:00:40.820 --> 00:00:45.130
The first season is 10 episodes long, and
is directed by a dynamic duo known as "Raj

00:00:45.130 --> 00:00:45.620
and DK."

00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:50.080
They've made a name for themselves in Bollywood
directing quirky sleepers like the 2011 crime

00:00:50.080 --> 00:00:54.120
drama Shor in the City and the 2013 zombie
comedy Goa Goa Gone.

00:00:54.230 --> 00:00:58.220
Amazon Prime doesn't have a firm release date
for the series premiere, but we know it'll

00:00:58.240 --> 00:00:59.620
be available in September.

00:01:00.420 --> 00:01:05.059
Starring Rosa Salazar of Alita: Battle Angel
fame and Bob Odenkirk of Better Call Saul,

00:01:05.059 --> 00:01:09.030
Amazon Prime's Undone is a unique animated
series about a woman whose sense of reality

00:01:09.030 --> 00:01:11.660
suffers a seismic shift after a car crash.

00:01:11.780 --> 00:01:16.580
Salazar's Alma wakes in her hospital bed to
find her dead father Jacob, played by Odenkirk,

00:01:16.580 --> 00:01:17.240
waiting for her.

00:01:17.340 --> 00:01:22.140
As the series unfolds, Alma's father reveals
she's experiencing time in a new, non-linear

00:01:22.140 --> 00:01:26.290
way, and he teaches her to use it so she can
solve the mystery of who killed him in the

00:01:26.290 --> 00:01:29.240
hopes she can eventually go back in time to
prevent his murder.

00:01:29.300 --> 00:01:32.600
Undone will be ready to blow your mind Friday,
September 13th.

00:01:32.740 --> 00:01:36.479
And now for a look at some of the best movies
coming to Prime in September, starting with

00:01:36.479 --> 00:01:37.960
the best action flicks on offer.

00:01:38.960 --> 00:01:42.969
Most of the television series added to Amazon
Prime's streaming service in September will

00:01:42.969 --> 00:01:47.420
be original content like Undone and The Family
Man, with the notable exception of American

00:01:47.420 --> 00:01:52.030
Horror Story: Apocalypse the eighth season
of the popular FX horror anthology series.

00:01:52.030 --> 00:01:55.479
Apocalypse begins with, true to its name,
a nuclear apocalypse.

00:01:55.480 --> 00:01:58.880
The series' stars are left in a decimated
world they have to learn to survive.

00:01:59.060 --> 00:02:02.100
See how or if they learn to cope on September
24th.

00:02:02.940 --> 00:02:07.460
September on Amazon Prime features car chases
at the end of the world, gunsmoke, epic duels,

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:10.670
and an American president beating up Gary
Oldman on a plane.

00:02:10.670 --> 00:02:14.890
All of the best action films are added to
Prime on the same day Monday, September 30th.

00:02:14.890 --> 00:02:19.510
At the end of July, George Miller revealed
there are multiple sequels to 2015's Mad Max:

00:02:19.510 --> 00:02:20.700
Fury Road in development.

00:02:20.890 --> 00:02:24.580
But if you're more a fan of the original films
starring Mel Gibson as the post-apocalyptic

00:02:24.590 --> 00:02:30.610
tough guy, Amazon Prime adds 1981's Mad Max
2: The Road Warrior and 1985's Mad Max Beyond

00:02:30.610 --> 00:02:32.320
Thunderdome to its library.

00:02:32.320 --> 00:02:35.570
If you like your future action flicks with
at least a little less apocalypse, Arnold

00:02:35.570 --> 00:02:40.200
Schwarzenegger gets his butt to Mars in 1990's
trippy action classic Total Recall.

00:02:40.580 --> 00:02:43.100
"If I'm not me, then who the hell am I?"

00:02:43.300 --> 00:02:47.580
Meanwhile, Kurt Russell and James Spader star
in the film that spawned a whole host of television

00:02:47.580 --> 00:02:49.880
spinoffs 1994's Stargate.

00:02:50.100 --> 00:02:54.780
On the same day, Harrison Ford stars as President
James Marshall who's kidnapped by the vengeful

00:02:54.780 --> 00:03:00.290
Gary Oldman in 1997's Air Force One, and Jon
Travolta and Nicolas Cage assume each others'

00:03:00.290 --> 00:03:03.160
identities in the John Woo classic Face/Off.

00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:07.280
Even though Halloween won't be for another
month, Amazon Prime isn't wasting any time

00:03:07.280 --> 00:03:08.440
in going for the screams.

00:03:08.600 --> 00:03:12.960
September 30th will see a long list of horror
and thriller flicks added to Prime's streaming

00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:13.460
library.

00:03:13.540 --> 00:03:18.420
If you enjoy your chills with a dash of science
fiction, there's 1997's Event Horizon starring

00:03:18.420 --> 00:03:20.040
Laurence Fishburne and Sam Neill.

00:03:20.280 --> 00:03:24.540
In early August we learned Death Note director
Adam Wingard was tapped to direct an upcoming

00:03:24.540 --> 00:03:28.760
TV series based on the film, so here's your
chance to check out the source material.

00:03:28.900 --> 00:03:33.100
For more earthbound terrors, there's 2008's
Cloverfield, following a group of friends

00:03:33.100 --> 00:03:35.740
trying to survive a giant monster attack in
New York City.

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:40.940
If you're more interested in thrillers rooted
in the real world, there's 2002's Insomnia.

00:03:40.940 --> 00:03:45.100
Directed by Christopher Nolan, Insomnia tells
the story of a sleep-deprived detective played

00:03:45.100 --> 00:03:49.750
by Al Pacino who accidentally shoots and kills
his own partner while pursuing suspected killer

00:03:49.750 --> 00:03:51.900
Walter Finch, played by Robin Williams.

00:03:52.120 --> 00:03:55.600
Prime's library will also include a number
of excellent psychological thrillers at the

00:03:55.610 --> 00:04:00.380
end of September, including 1999's The Talented
Mr. Ripley starring Matt Damon and Gwyneth

00:04:00.380 --> 00:04:05.880
Paltrow and 2003's Gothika starring Halle
Berry and future Iron Man Robert Downey Jr.

00:04:06.100 --> 00:04:12.880
"I suggest that we simply increase the medication
until things start to make sense."

00:04:12.880 --> 00:04:16.420
"Or maybe until I can get myself a new doctor."

00:04:17.020 --> 00:04:21.919
For more dramatic fare, Amazon Prime's September
30th offerings bring war, thunder, ghosts

00:04:21.920 --> 00:04:22.460
and grit.

00:04:22.680 --> 00:04:27.960
Ethan and Joel Cohen's excellent 2010 remake
of 1969 classic True Grit will be available

00:04:27.960 --> 00:04:32.590
for streaming, starring Jeff Bridges as the
drunken curmudgeon Rooster Cogburn, and Hailee

00:04:32.590 --> 00:04:34.580
Steinfeld as the young Mattie Ross.

00:04:34.800 --> 00:04:38.650
For an epic much closer chronologically to
our own time, there's Oliver Stone's Vietnam

00:04:38.650 --> 00:04:43.720
War saga Platoon, starring Charlie Sheen and
an incredible ensemble cast, including Willem

00:04:43.720 --> 00:04:44.220
Dafoe.

00:04:44.440 --> 00:04:48.520
If you're excited about the upcoming sequel
no one was expecting, Top Gun: Maverick, you

00:04:48.521 --> 00:04:53.009
might be able to satisfy your cravings a bit
with the 1990 sports action drama Days of

00:04:53.009 --> 00:04:57.790
Thunder starring Tom Cruise as stock car racer
Cole Trickle and Nicole Kidman as Trickle's

00:04:57.790 --> 00:04:59.700
neurosurgeon love interest Claire.

00:04:59.920 --> 00:05:04.060
If you want something without so much car
racing or war, there's 2001's black comedy

00:05:04.061 --> 00:05:09.710
drama Ghost World, starring Thora Birch, Steve
Buscemi, and future Avenger Scarlett Johansson.

00:05:09.710 --> 00:05:11.840
"You just hate every single guy on the face
of the Earth."

00:05:11.980 --> 00:05:12.780
"That's not true.

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:16.640
I just hate all these extroverted, pseudo-bohemian
losers."

00:05:16.740 --> 00:05:18.040
"You guys up for some reggae tonight?"

00:05:19.280 --> 00:05:22.980
There isn't a lot of comedy on its way to
Amazon Prime in September, but what is coming

00:05:22.980 --> 00:05:25.860
is interesting — and it all drops on September
30th.

00:05:26.020 --> 00:05:30.100
Prime may be one of the few places you'll
be able to see 1994's Trading Mom.

00:05:30.260 --> 00:05:35.259
Starring Sissy Spacek of Carrie fame and Anna
Chlumsky of My Girl and Veep, Trading Mom

00:05:35.260 --> 00:05:39.680
is about a trio of siblings who cast a spell
on their nagging mother to make her disappear.

00:05:39.810 --> 00:05:43.980
For a comedy fantasy that's a bit more recent,
there's 2008's Ghost Town, starring Ricky

00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:48.240
Gervais in his first leading film role as
a dentist who can see and communicate with

00:05:48.240 --> 00:05:48.740
ghosts.

00:05:48.940 --> 00:05:50.880
Check out one of our newest videos right here!

00:05:50.940 --> 00:05:54.220
Plus, even more Looper videos about your favorite
movies are coming soon.

00:05:54.520 --> 00:05:58.500
Subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit the
bell so you don't miss a single one.

